; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Rain Shower
; CATEGORY: Animation & Many Turtles
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     animation, CLEAN, REMAINDER, loops, weather
; SUMMARY:  Animates slanting rain falling from a grey cloud onto a puddle, frame by frame.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A heavy cloud hangs over a green field. Sixty raindrops slant
;   down out of it and splash into a puddle. When a drop reaches the
;   ground it wraps around to the top again, so the rain never
;   stops.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Press Stop to end it. Change :wind to blow the rain.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a frame counter that grows by one each picture
;   * REMAINDER to wrap a number around (like a clock)
;   * giving each drop its own place from its number, no lists needed
;   * CLEAN and redraw for smooth animation
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make :wind 0 for rain that falls straight down.
;   * Make the drops fall faster by changing 9 in DROP.
;   * Add a flash of lightning now and then with SETBACKGROUND.
; ============================================================

; SCENE draws the field, the puddle and the cloud.
to scene
  setpencolor [70 130 70] setpensize 100
  penup setxy -400 -260 setheading 90 pendown forward 800
  ; A very thick line has round ends, which makes a nice puddle.
  setpencolor [90 110 150] setpensize 30
  penup setxy -120 -250 pendown forward 240
  ; The cloud is a bunch of overlapping grey dots.
  setpencolor [110 110 120] setpensize 120
  foreach [-160 -60 40 140] [dot list ? 200]
  setpensize 90
  foreach [-110 -10 90] [dot list ? 240]
end

; DROP draws raindrop number :k at frame :t. Its x is spread out by
; multiplying its number, and it falls 9 steps every frame. REMAINDER
; keeps the height between 0 and 400, so the drop loops forever.
to drop :k :t
  localmake "x remainder :k * 137 600
  localmake "fall remainder :t * 9 + :k * 53 400
  localmake "y 180 - :fall
  penup setxy :x - 300 + :wind * :fall / 10 :y pendown
  setheading 180 + :wind
  forward 14
end

; FRAME draws one picture of the rain.
to frame :t
  clean
  scene
  setpencolor [170 200 255]
  setpensize 2
  for [k 1 60] [drop :k :t]
  wait 2
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [160 170 185]
make "wind 15
make "t 0
forever [
  frame :t
  make "t :t + 1
]
